-- title:
--   Lemma B.7 — potential and simultaneous product inequalities: $\mathbb E\Psi_T\le e^{1/16}$, $\mathbb EU<1$, pathwise certificates, supermartingale
-- statement:
--   Run SHARP with design horizon $T\ge2$, resolution $\gamma\in\Gamma_T$, nets satisfying (B.3) and a fixed Borel response selector with error $1/T$, against any adversary of the tagged experiment. Let $m_j=|\{t:J_t=j\}|$, $S_c=\sum_tf_{c,t}$ and
--   $$U=\log(1+\Psi_T),\qquad\lambda_k=\log\big(3n_k(k+1)2^{k+2}\big)+U,\qquad\lambda^{\mathrm{ctr}}_0=\log8+U .$$
--   Then $\mathbb E\Psi_T\le e^{1/16}$ and $\mathbb EU\le\log(1+e^{1/16})<1$. Pathwise, for every boundary constraint $c$ at level $k$ and every $\eta\in H_k$,
--   $$S_c\le4\eta m_{j(c)}+\lambda_k/\eta ,$$
--   the same holds for each centre constraint with $\eta=\gamma/16$ and budget $\lambda^{\mathrm{ctr}}_0$, and all these budgets exceed one. With $\alpha_T=1+1/(16T)$, $(\Psi_t/\alpha_T^t)_{t=0}^T$ is a nonnegative $(\mathcal F_t)$-supermartingale starting at one.
--
--   One potential thus controls every constraint at every rate simultaneously, with no union bound.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: SHARP (Algorithm 4.1, Eqs. (B.18)–(B.24)) in the canonical tagged experiment of §A.3 → `sharpLaw sel D T`: the tagged law of the Sharp/TagExperiment definitions; weights as closed-form products; tag draw `∑_j q_t(j) δ_j`; reason: the product form equals the recursion (B.21); the law is the ordered-kernel law of §A.3
--   - encoding: γ ∈ Γ_T = {2^{−k} : 0 ≤ k ≤ ⌊log₂ T⌋} → γ = `gam ell` = 2^{−ℓ} with `ell ≤ Nat.log 2 T`; reason: the same set of resolutions, indexed by ℓ_γ = log₂(1/γ)
--   - encoding: angular r_s-nets X_s ⊆ S¹ with |X_s| ≤ 16/r_s (Eq. (B.3)), angular distance = shorter arc → `NetsOK ell X`: `X k` a `Finset` of unit vectors, every unit `u` within `arccos ⟨u, x⟩ ≤ r_k` of some `x ∈ X k`, and `card (X k) ≤ 16 / r_k`; reason: arccos⟨u, x⟩ is the length of the shorter arc between unit vectors; same nets
--   - encoding: tags J = {0} ∪ {(s, x)}, constraints h_c of Eqs. (B.6)–(B.7) → `Tag ell X = Option (Σ k, X k)` (`none` = 0); `hval c g = hconst c + ⟨hvec c, g⟩`; centre constraints indexed by `(i, σ) ∈ Fin 2 × Bool` (0-based coordinate, `true` = +1); reason: the same tags and the same affine maps
--   - generalization: any fixed Borel response selector satisfying Proposition B.3 with error at most 1/T → any `sel` with `IsResponseSelector (1/T) sel`: Borel, Δ(J)-valued on Δ(C), with L_κ(sel κ, g) ≤ 1/T (Eq. (B.12)); dyadic coordinates not required; reason: only (B.12) is used by SHARP's analysis; a selector with dyadic coordinates (the B.3 selector) is a special case
--   - generalization: uniformly over admissible adversaries → every `TagAdversary`: kernels on the tag–loss history (past tags, losses, hence every past announcement, past point and the current tag law q_t); reason: this is the stronger adversary the upper-bound analysis permits (p. 14, §A.3); every adversary of the public protocol is one, by composing its kernels with the map from tag–loss histories to public histories
--   - encoding: E[·] and P{·} under the canonical law → Bochner integrals and measures of events under `law`/`sharpLaw` (`ENNReal.ofReal p ≤ μ {…}` for P{…} ≥ p); reason: the integrands are bounded Borel functions (Proposition A.1); same values
--   - encoding: pathwise → for every tag–loss history h ∈ (J × B²₂)^T; reason: the inequalities are deterministic in the realized transcript
--   - encoding: (Ψ_t/α_T^t) is a nonnegative (F_t)-supermartingale starting at one → Ψ_0 = 1, nonnegativity, integrability, and ∫_A M_{t+1} ≤ ∫_A M_t for every A ∈ F_t = σ(first t rounds), t < T; reason: the definition of a supermartingale; M_t is a function of the first t rounds, so it is adapted
-- source:
--   Saravanan, Minimax Realized Full Swap Regret on the Euclidean Disk, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 e7138cc2…), p. 26, Lemma B.7

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SwapDisk_Main_TagExperiment

open MeasureTheory

namespace SwapDisk.Main

/-- Lemma B.7 (Potential and simultaneous product inequalities), p. 26, for SHARP with design
horizon `T`, resolution `γ = 2^{−ℓ} ∈ Γ_T`, any nets satisfying (B.3) and any Borel response
selector with error `1/T`, against every adversary that sees past tags: `EΨ_T ≤ e^{1/16}`,
`EU ≤ log(1 + e^{1/16}) < 1`; pathwise, `S_c ≤ 4η m_{j(c)} + λ_k/η` for every boundary
constraint at level `k` and `η ∈ H_k`, and with `η = γ/16`, budget `λ^ctr_0` at the centre; all
budgets exceed one; `(Ψ_t/α_T^t)_{t=0}^T`, `α_T = 1 + 1/(16T)`, is a nonnegative
`(F_t)`-supermartingale starting at one (`F_t` generated by all coordinates of the first `t`
rounds). -/
theorem lemma_B_7 (T ell : ℕ) (hT : 2 ≤ T) (hell : ell ≤ Nat.log 2 T)
    (X : Fin (ell + 1) → Finset E2) (hX : NetsOK ell X)
    (sel : (Con ell X → ℝ) → (Tag ell X → ℝ)) (hsel : IsResponseSelector (1 / (T : ℝ)) sel)
    (D : TagAdversary (Tag ell X)) :
    ∫ z, Psi (TagTraj.hist z) ∂(sharpLaw sel D T) ≤ Real.exp (1 / 16) ∧
    ∫ z, Ubudget (TagTraj.hist z) ∂(sharpLaw sel D T) ≤ Real.log (1 + Real.exp (1 / 16)) ∧
    Real.log (1 + Real.exp (1 / 16)) < 1 ∧
    (∀ h : Fin T → Tag ell X × Disk,
      (∀ (b : BTag ell X) (κd : BKind) (l : ℕ), l ≤ (b.1 : ℕ) →
        certSum h (.inr (b, κd)) ≤
          4 * (scale ell b.1 * (2 : ℝ) ^ (-(l : ℤ)) / 16) * tagCount (fun u => (h u).1) (some b) +
            lamB h b.1 / (scale ell b.1 * (2 : ℝ) ^ (-(l : ℤ)) / 16)) ∧
      (∀ a : Fin 2 × Bool,
        certSum h (.inl a) ≤
          4 * (gam ell / 16) * tagCount (fun u => (h u).1) none + lamCtr h / (gam ell / 16)) ∧
      (∀ k : Fin (ell + 1), 1 < lamB h k) ∧ 1 < lamCtr h) ∧
    (∀ z : TagTraj (Tag ell X) D T,
      Psi (TagTraj.hist (TagTraj.prefix 0 (Nat.zero_le T) z)) = 1) ∧
    (∀ (t : ℕ) (ht : t ≤ T), ∀ z : TagTraj (Tag ell X) D T,
      0 ≤ Psi (TagTraj.hist (TagTraj.prefix t ht z)) / (1 + 1 / (16 * (T : ℝ))) ^ t) ∧
    (∀ (t : ℕ) (ht : t ≤ T),
      Integrable (fun z => Psi (TagTraj.hist (TagTraj.prefix t ht z)) /
        (1 + 1 / (16 * (T : ℝ))) ^ t) (sharpLaw sel D T)) ∧
    ∀ (t : ℕ) (ht : t + 1 ≤ T) (A : Set (TagTraj (Tag ell X) D t)), MeasurableSet A →
      ∫ z in TagTraj.prefix t (Nat.le_of_succ_le ht) ⁻¹' A,
          Psi (TagTraj.hist (TagTraj.prefix (t + 1) ht z)) / (1 + 1 / (16 * (T : ℝ))) ^ (t + 1)
            ∂(sharpLaw sel D T) ≤
        ∫ z in TagTraj.prefix t (Nat.le_of_succ_le ht) ⁻¹' A,
          Psi (TagTraj.hist (TagTraj.prefix t (Nat.le_of_succ_le ht) z)) /
            (1 + 1 / (16 * (T : ℝ))) ^ t ∂(sharpLaw sel D T) := by sorry

end SwapDisk.Main
